In terms of resistance exercise frequency, the World Health Organization recommends that adults engage in muscle-strengthening activities on 2 or more days a week, targeting all major muscle groups. This is a general guideline and does not specify the exact amount of protein intake needed for optimal results in conjunction with resistance training.

